{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>His servant's eye.</b> A Canaanite slave — but a Hebrew slave does not go free for tooth and eye, as we have said: he does not go free in the manner of the [Canaanite] slaves." "<b>In place of his eye.</b> And likewise for twenty-four limb-tips: the fingertips of the hands and the feet, and the two ears, and the nose, and the tip of the torso — which is the membrum. And why are tooth and eye stated? For if eye were stated and tooth were not stated, I would say: just as the eye, which was created with him, so too everything that was created with him — but a tooth was not created with him. And if tooth were stated and eye were not stated, I would say: even a baby's tooth, which has a replacement. Therefore eye is stated (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:40.534681094Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}